version 0.1.0

// bench/bundle_size — the product-level bundle-size monitor (see README.md):
// measures live examples/ plus use-case importer benchmarks listed in
// cases.txt. #897 (ADR-0070): this directory sat outside the issue's
// originally-scoped `lib/@vibe/*` / `lib/@vibex/wasm/*` surface (Phase 3 only
// enumerated those two prefixes), so it was missed until Phase 4's
// `vibe check --missing-vpkg` CI gate caught it. Not wired into any script
// or Taskfile task today (grepped scripts/*.sh, scripts/*.py, Taskfile.pkl —
// zero hits), so this is a pure facade-shape fix, no behavioral risk.
//
// The consumer_*.vibe files are standalone benchmark entry scripts (each
// leaf-imports its own case from ./prelude/{double,option}.vibe and ends in
// a bare expression, compiled independently per cases.txt) -- they export
// nothing, but still need a mandatory facade dependency line per the #753
// implicit-membership convention (a plain sibling `.vibe` file with zero
// exports would otherwise have no import line at all).

